    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "JB Kelly presents Sebring, a detached coastal residence occupying a remarkable beachfront site on Claremont Strand, one of the most sought-after and picturesque locations on the Howth Peninsula. Set on approximately 0.4 acres with direct access onto the beach, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a home in an exceptional waterfront setting with uninterrupted views across Burrow Beach, Ireland's Eye, Howth Harbour and the wider coastline.\r\n\r\nThe property has been extensively renovated and carefully maintained over the years and enjoys a private, mature setting sheltered by established trees and planting. Accessed via a long private driveway, the house sits comfortably within its generous site, with substantial gardens to the front and rear enjoying sunlight throughout the day. The mature grounds provide a high degree of privacy while maintaining a strong connection to the surrounding coastal landscape.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is arranged to maximise the property's unique setting and sea views. Entry is provided through either a bright front sunroom or an extended sun lounge to the side. The principal accommodation comprises a kitchen/breakfast room and a living/dining room, both enjoying views towards the beach and sea. There are four bedrooms, a family bathroom and a large attached garage providing valuable storage and further potential. To the rear, mature tree-lined gardens create a sheltered and secluded outdoor environment. Enjoy day-long barbeques and outdoor living in a cozy summer chalet soaking up the afternoon to evening sun to the front.\r\n\r\nA defining feature of Sebring is the quality of its site. Extending to approximately 0.4 acres, the property offers obvious potential for further enhancement, extension or redevelopment, subject to planning permission. The combination of direct beach frontage, substantial grounds and uninterrupted coastal views is rarely available and will appeal to purchasers seeking either a long-term family home or a landmark coastal project.\r\n\r\nStepping directly from the rear garden onto Claremont Strand, owners can enjoy immediate access to one of Dublin's most scenic stretches of coastline. The ever-changing outlook across the bay provides a unique backdrop throughout the year, with views extending from Malahide and Ireland's Eye to Howth Harbour and the East Pier. Howth Village is within walking distance along the shoreline and offers a wide selection of restaurants, cafés, shops and marina facilities. The area is also well served by DART and bus connections, together with a range of sporting and recreational amenities.\r\n\r\nSebring represents a rare opportunity to acquire a private coastal home on a substantial beachfront site in one of Dublin's most prestigious waterfront locations. The exceptional setting, direct beach access and significant development potential combine to create a property of considerable long-term appeal."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Sunroom\r\n2.60 x 1.65m\r\nOverlooking front garden. Wooden floors, feature floor to ceiling windows with vaulted ceiling. Leading to front door.\r\n\r\nEntrance\r\n0.80 x 1.65m\r\nGlass panelling.\r\n\r\nHall\r\n1.80 x 3.40 + 1.00 x 4.30m\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\n2.45 x 3.15m\r\nOverlooking front garden. Fitted wardrobes\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n4.60 x 3.15m\r\nSeaviews. Fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\n3.00 x 3.15m\r\nOverlooking front garden.\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\n2.60 x 2.00m\r\nBath with shower over, WC, WHB, bidet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\n2.85 x 2.00\r\nSeaviews.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\n4.50 x 6.45m\r\nSea views. Marble open fireplace. Large floor-to-ceiling window and patio doors to rear garden. \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room\r\n3.05 x 6.45m\r\nSeaviews. Laminate flooring, tiled flooring in kitchen area. Range of floor and wall-mounted presses. Dishwasher. \r\n\r\nSide Sun Lounge\r\n2.10 x 4.95m\r\nOverlooking front garden. Floor-to-wall glazed sliding doors and windows. Tiled floors. Feature glazed vaulted roof light with downlighting surround.\r\n\r\nUtility Room\r\n2.10 x 2.75m\r\nGuest WC. Door to rear garden."
